WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.360
We had five people here.

2
00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:04.900
I was more worried about them five people, because I gave them body bags before I left.

3
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.160
I said, "I'm going to give you a body bag because this is serious."

4
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.320
I gave them the keys to the city hall, and they saved their lives in here.

5
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:18.160
But in the back of my mind is saying . . . I put my hand on the Bible and I told God that I was going to do the right thing.

6
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.920
And, "God, don't let me lose a life."

7
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.940
But one of the hardest things is to ask you to leave, as mayor, and you're telling me, "I'm not leaving."

8
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.400
And I can't make you leave, even though it's mandatory.

9
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.720
I made all kinds of deals with everybody I can.

10
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:37.740
I had twenty-six of them and only . . . I got every . . . twenty-one of them out except for five.

11
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.600
And they wanted to stay.

12
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:46.800
So when you remembered that when you got word back, it was like back in Betsy, it was back Andrew, all the storms.

13
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.340
"Oh, man, Grand Isle's wiped out."

14
00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:52.580
Now if you're sitting in North Louisiana, evacuated, you said, "Oh my God, we lost everything."

15
00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:57.220
I'll remind you, after Betsy, they raised up the houses eight feet.

16
00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.800
After Andrew, they went up twelve feet.

17
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.720
After Katrina, it's an average of fifteen feet.
